<section image-layout="blank" id="jL1lOY6k91" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sWVnWz4V8U" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Agricultural machinery efficiency</p><h1 font-size="40pt">The efficiency of agricultural machinery: why utilization beats horsepower</h1><p font-size="lg">A technical workbook for choosing and operating agricultural tools and machinery, or alsintan, by capacity, cost per hectare and work actually completed.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Field measurement · ownership arithmetic · one reproducible case</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3rXNzwCDPS" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/GPmwQspv1177jcGdV3sHM.png" saved-media-id="weofxxop3y60tnd" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Elevated documentary agricultural photograph of an unbranded rice transplanter working precise parallel passes across a wet paddy, headland turns clearly visible, neutral overcast daylight, crisp soil and crop texture, carbon-black machinery with restrained signal-red details, no text, no logos, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="MicuMfZ9ol" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="H1ZvY6AK8U"><h2 style="padding-right: 18%;">A machine that sits idle is more expensive than no machine at all</h2><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 20%;">Purchase price and engine power do not determine cost per hectare. Annual ownership cost stays fixed; every additional hectare spreads that cost further.</p><spacer size="22pt"></spacer><display size="md">Rp 1,023,000 → Rp 666,000</display><h4>per hectare, with the same transplanter</h4><p>The machine did not change. The working calendar did. The following arithmetic separates field capacity, annual utilization and loss avoided.</p><p role="caption">Ownership-cost method: <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">Ontario Ministry of Agriculture</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="YeLoXAcMlS" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="G7ia8yj9gX"><h2>"Efficiency" hides three separate questions — measure all three</h2><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" padding-top="40pt"><grid-item id="CGylMnBLjb" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/TntEzmEMZwRCgPTLV0Q7.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="field route clock efficiency" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black field or empty space enclosed by a white boundary, symbolizing a void, area, or region.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Field efficiency</h3><p>What share of field time is actual work rather than turning, refilling or waiting?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uUea5xJl67" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/0YFFyWmxPkwK8QlCzhcI.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="calculator cost per hectare" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A basic calculator symbol consisting of a box with buttons or a panel on top and a display screen at the top, used for simple mathematical calculations.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Cost efficiency</h3><p>What is the fixed plus variable cost per hectare at real annual use?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YLbLC92VDv" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/CWoZw8wMw76hzAHan9vyNt.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="grain sack labor time" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black grain silhouette against a white background, representing the concept of grain.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Loss and labor</h3><p>How much grain is saved and how many workdays are released per hectare?</p></grid-item></grid><p><b>High capacity can still fail economically when the machine is chronically underused.</b></p><p role="caption">Methods: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">Iowa State field capacity</a> · <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">machinery costs</a> · <a href="https://epublikasi.pertanian.go.id/berkala/jae/article/view/3633">harvest loss</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="3J2SLtSlJk"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Mg21HkAoxT"><h2>Field capacity: the one formula the rest of the deck rests on</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="qz9YYVC2g5" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><p role="eyebrow">Theoretical capacity</p><formula>C_t=\frac{v\times w}{10}</formula><p><math>v</math> is speed in km/h; <math>w</math> is working width in metres. The result is hectares per hour.</p><p role="eyebrow">Effective capacity</p><formula>C_e=C_t\times\eta_f</formula><p><math>\eta_f</math> includes headland turns, refuelling and refilling.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="1deykRX9A-" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="35"><labels><label variant="solid">Worked example</label></labels><h3>Subsoiler, 10-hour day</h3><p>5 km/h × 2 m ÷ 10 = <b>1.0 ha/h theoretical</b></p><p>17% time lost → field efficiency = <b>0.83</b></p><p>1.0 × 0.83 = <b>0.83 ha/h effective</b></p><p>0.83 × 10 hours = <b>8.3 ha/day</b></p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Typical field efficiencies: plows 78–85%; tandem disk ~80–83%; fertilizer spreader ~70%. Sources: <a href="https://www.nda.gov.za/images/Branches/Economica%20Development%20Trade%20and%20Marketing/Statistc%20and%20%20Economic%20Analysis/economic-analysis/2015-2016-guide-to-machinery-costs-field-capacity-explain-table-.pdf">field-capacity guide</a> · <a href="https://www.computus.co.za/Publikasies/machA1.pdf">machinery tables</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Y4ruRPMTcQ"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="NlvBWwOoPH"><h2>A measured Indonesian machine: the Indo Jarwo transplanter at 86%</h2><p>Field tests on 10 × 10 m plots in Pinrang, South Sulawesi, compared three operating speeds.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="9zDjUNkcq6" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">1.52</display><h4>km/h</h4><p>Best working speed in the trial.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BFfIG9qIWL" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">0.14 → 0.12</display><h4>ha/hour</h4><p>Theoretical capacity to effective capacity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="qf2lA_wxgY" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">86%</display><h4>Field efficiency</h4><p>0.12 ÷ 0.14; one hectare takes 8.33 hours.</p></grid-item></grid><p>A separately measured BBP Mektan manual transplanter reached <b>86.79%</b>, with <b>4.2%</b> of time lost. Reproduce the test: time one pass, measure its width and count the turns.</p><p role="caption">Sources: <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">Pinrang Indo Jarwo field test</a> · <a href="http://repository.pertanian.go.id/handle/123456789/2046?show=full">BBP Mektan study</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="PHm36zgrgx" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="large"><grid-item id="aym_3ti05M" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="lg">14%</display><h2>Where the missing 14% goes — and which parts you can buy back</h2><p>Plot geometry and logistics set most of the gap. More engine power does not shorten a headland turn or move seedlings closer to the machine.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="iPFK85YD5Y" vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><custom-code>
        <style>
          .field-loss-map{font-family:var(--body-font);color:var(--body-color);width:100%}
          .field-loss-map svg{width:100%;height:20em;display:block}
          .field-loss-map text{font-family:var(--body-font);fill:var(--body-color);font-size:.72em}
          .field-loss-map .label{font-family:var(--heading-font);font-weight:700;font-size:.78em}
          .field-loss-map .field{fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--body-color) 4%,transparent);stroke:var(--body-color);stroke-width:1.5}
          .field-loss-map .pass{stroke:color-mix(in srgb,var(--body-color) 35%,transparent);stroke-width:2}
          .field-loss-map .loss{stroke:var(--accent-color);fill:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent-color) 13%,transparent);stroke-width:3}
          .field-loss-map .route{stroke:var(--accent-color);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:7 6;fill:none}
          .field-loss-map .rule{stroke:var(--body-color);stroke-width:1}
        </style>
        <div class="field-loss-map">
          <svg width="560" height="320" viewBox="0 0 560 320" role="img" aria-label="Overhead field plan showing four sources of lost working time">
            <rect class="field" x="92" y="40" width="300" height="232" rx="3"></rect>
            <line class="pass" x1="118" y1="64" x2="118" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="154" y1="64" x2="154" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="190" y1="64" x2="190" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="226" y1="64" x2="226" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="262" y1="64" x2="262" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="298" y1="64" x2="298" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="334" y1="64" x2="334" y2="248"></line>
            <line class="pass" x1="370" y1="64" x2="370" y2="248"></line>
            <rect class="loss" x="92" y="40" width="300" height="25"></rect>
            <rect class="loss" x="92" y="247" width="300" height="25"></rect>
            <circle class="loss" cx="92" cy="116" r="12"></circle>
            <circle class="loss" cx="226" cy="160" r="12"></circle>
            <rect class="field" x="452" y="205" width="78" height="67" rx="3"></rect>
            <path class="route" d="M392 235 C420 235 420 235 452 235"></path>
            <line class="rule" x1="70" y1="67" x2="20" y2="67"></line>
            <text class="label" x="8" y="52">Headland turning</text>
            <text x="8" y="67">Longer, squarer runs</text>
            <line class="rule" x1="92" y1="116" x2="18" y2="116"></line>
            <text class="label" x="8" y="101">Refilling</text>
            <text x="8" y="131">Stage inputs here</text>
            <line class="rule" x1="238" y1="160" x2="430" y2="160"></line>
            <text class="label" x="438" y="149">Adjustment</text>
            <text x="438" y="165">Train clearing</text>
            <text x="438" y="181">and setup</text>
            <text class="label" x="405" y="294">Transport between plots</text>
            <text x="405" y="309">Consumes the working day</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </custom-code></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="yvzrqRGyPC"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="LzOElTcTIh" colspan="42"><h2>Five use stages, five efficiency traps</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="5dvG976hiU" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Land preparation</h4><p font-size="sm">A hand tractor produced up to 15× the output of manual hoeing in measured trials.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OKDT8LH6vr" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Planting</h4><p font-size="sm">Manual seeding-to-planting used 32.79 male and 23.79 female hours/ha, against 18.67 male hours/ha mechanized.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hWpdjhUdLK" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Crop care</h4><p font-size="sm">Power weeders and sprayers delivered about 10× manual weeding output.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J0I-4sCFUk" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Harvest</h4><p font-size="sm">A combine used three workers and about five hours per hectare.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="MHFVNi7qIH" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Post-harvest</h4><p font-size="sm">Thresher output reached about 17× manual output.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><span text-color="muted">Sources: </span><a href="https://repository.pertanian.go.id/bitstreams/3b4f6e92-594f-4dda-820e-e45545382b3b/download">mechanization trials</a><span text-color="muted"> · </span><a href="https://doi.org/10.20961/sepa.v10i1.13958">planting labor</a><span text-color="muted"> · </span><a href="https://repository.ummat.ac.id/6179/">combine labor</a><span text-color="muted">.</span></p></grid-item><grid-item id="MvQYjsRcVS" padding="0" colspan="18"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/K559VAWvNEOTzFstmouVu.png" saved-media-id="lg12q2hp5ixgpth" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Documentary agricultural photograph of several unbranded implements staged in working order at the edge of a rice field, hand tractor, transplanter attachment, crop-care implement and compact harvesting equipment visible as a practical operating sequence, elevated technical viewpoint, neutral overcast daylight, machine gray and carbon-black metal with restrained signal-red details, no logos, no text, no identifiable people" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="2UXkaQOfDW"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="JXyATtiLGM" padding="0" colspan="20"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/7nTsqfG9g5uUS-JnHgp6m.png" saved-media-id="vvx1sgbdasimbmm" source="image.ai-generated" fill="true" image-style="technical-field-documentary" alt="Close technical documentary photograph of an operator's gloved hands inspecting the hitch, drive components and adjustment points of an unbranded agricultural implement before purchase, neutral workshop-field edge, overcast daylight, machine gray metal, carbon-black shadows and one restrained signal-red inspection tag, no text, no logos, no identifiable face" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="DCQiiwIg8s" colspan="40"><h2>Choosing the machine: six checks before the purchase order</h2><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="symbol" marker-label="✓" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 26pt; --marker-gap: 10pt;"><grid-item id="IwCTufBrKj" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Match power to the heaviest task</h4><p font-size="sm">Undersized units finish late and wear fast.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sQkqLPlvYE" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Test plot size and shape</h4><p font-size="sm">Fragmentation caps field efficiency.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5q0Lxh8hHa" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Check soil and water condition</h4><p font-size="sm">Puddled paddy, dry upland and peat need different traction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sc6CdWNLvm" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Estimate annual area</h4><p font-size="sm">Compare it with break-even before committing.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="0T6JOT3kze" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Confirm local support</h4><p font-size="sm">Service, spare parts and operator skill must be within reach.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="XKxQApaGW0" padding="6pt 8pt" colspan="30"><h4 font-size="16pt">Price the hiring alternative</h4><p font-size="sm">Hire when the local rate beats ownership cost per hectare.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="11pt"><span text-color="#5A6068">Decision methods: </span><a href="http://arhiva.nara.ac.rs/handle/123456789/1591">break-even area</a><span text-color="#5A6068"> · </span><a href="https://farmdocdaily.illinois.edu/wp-content/uploads/2017/09/fdd010917.pdf">own versus custom hire</a><span text-color="#5A6068">.</span></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="GRBV-iR8yd" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="7x39UAx28B"><h2>Cost splits in two, and only one half responds to use</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="wKg9RrdyX4" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">Fixed ownership cost</label></labels><h3>Unchanged at 5 ha or 50 ha</h3><p>Depreciation, interest, insurance and housing are paid by the year.</p><formula>D=\frac{\text{purchase price}-\text{salvage value}}{\text{optimal life}}</formula></grid-item><grid-item id="UetnwaVnob" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="outline">Variable operating cost</label></labels><h3>Roughly constant per hectare</h3><p>Fuel, lubricant, repairs and operator wages rise with the work completed.</p><p>The engine affects this half. Utilization controls how the fixed half is spread.</p></grid-item></grid><formula>\text{Cost per hectare}=\frac{\text{annual fixed cost}}{\text{hectares worked}}+\text{variable cost per hectare}</formula><p><b>Hectares worked are the denominator. That division is the whole utilization argument.</b></p><p role="caption">Cost categories and depreciation method: <a href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/budgeting-farm-machinery-costs">machinery-cost guide</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="UKhnYn-4SK"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="cinHFOdapr"><h2>Break-even area: the number that decides buy or hire</h2><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="Ztqk2xqwfM" vertical-align="center" colspan="39"><graph chart-type="line" y-axis-min="0" text-size="md" width="550pt" height="270pt"><properties><property key="hectares" label="Hectares per year" type="label"></property><property key="fixed" label="Fixed · Rp '000/ha" type="data"></property><property key="variable" label="Variable · Rp '000/ha" type="data"></property><property key="total" label="Total · Rp '000/ha" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>10</cell><cell>1286</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>1666</cell></row><row><cell>20</cell><cell>643</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>1023</cell></row><row><cell>30</cell><cell>429</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>809</cell></row><row><cell>40</cell><cell>322</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>702</cell></row><row><cell>50</cell><cell>257</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>637</cell></row><row><cell>60</cell><cell>214</cell><cell>380</cell><cell>594</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption">Illustrative transplanter cost curve. Fixed cost per hectare collapses with use; variable cost stays flat.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BZFWJFSKAI" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="21"><p role="eyebrow">Decision rule</p><formula>A_{BE}=\frac{F}{R_c-V}</formula><p>Below break-even area, owning costs more per hectare than custom hiring.</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><display size="md">13.46 <span font-size="18pt">ha/year</span></display><p>Sijunjung: modified manual transplanter Rp 325,057/ha; manual planting Rp 653,343/ha.</p><p font-size="sm"><a href="http://repository.pertanian.go.id/handle/123456789/2046?show=full"><b>Measured Sijunjung case</b></a>.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="PWMmhq7ZYn"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="iXJWU0xv31"><h2>Harvest loss is efficiency you can weigh in the sack</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="c6gc-010KE" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><display size="md">200.39</display><h4>kg/ha saved in Banten</h4><p>Matched samples found combine harvesters reduced loss by about 3.52% of yield.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="m0FidDm-R8" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><display size="md">0.43%</display><h4>Combine loss in Sumbawa</h4><p>Manual loss was 1.03%/ha. Production cost was Rp 9.33 million/ha versus Rp 11.27 million/ha.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YErkKpobrm" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><display size="md">4.9%</display><h4>Total loss in North Sulawesi</h4><p>A Kubota DC70 Plus trial measured 4.7% scattered during cutting alone.</p></grid-item></grid><aside variant="caution"><p><b>Define the boundary before comparing machines.</b> These studies count different components of harvest loss.</p></aside><p role="caption">Sources: <a href="https://epublikasi.pertanian.go.id/berkala/jae/article/view/3633">Banten</a> · <a href="https://eprints.unram.ac.id/31651/">Sumbawa</a> · <a href="https://ejournal.unsrat.ac.id/v3/index.php/teta/article/download/51068/44083/121028">North Sulawesi</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="WqABaoXQ1l"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="oiOL_0ed4Z"><h2>Seven indicators worth tracking every season</h2><table col-widths="[28,26,46]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Indicator</p></td><td><p>Unit</p></td><td><p>How to calculate or use it</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Effective field capacity</b></p></td><td><p>ha/hour</p></td><td><p>Actual area ÷ actual field hours.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Field efficiency</b></p></td><td><p>%</p></td><td><p>Effective capacity ÷ theoretical capacity.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Utilization</b></p></td><td><p>ha/year</p></td><td><p>Compare directly with break-even area.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Cost per hectare</b></p></td><td><p>Rp/ha</p></td><td><p>Recalculate fixed plus variable cost every year.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Harvest or process loss</b></p></td><td><p>%</p></td><td><p>Weigh it; do not estimate it.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Fuel per hectare</b></p></td><td><p>litres/ha</p></td><td><p>Use increases as an early maintenance warning.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Downtime</b></p></td><td><p>% of scheduled days</p></td><td><p>Shows where the working season is actually lost.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p role="caption">Field-capacity definitions: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">Iowa State University Extension</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="LCU52TqX7S"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="wX0xEUdj7K"><h2>Case study: UPJA Tani Makmur buys a transplanter</h2><aside icon="false"><p font-size="sm"><b>Illustrative example — a fictional farmer-group service unit with reproducible constructed figures, not a real cooperative.</b></p></aside><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="wx8tHdJWzn" colspan="36"><h3>Ownership inputs</h3><table col-widths="[37,63]" header-row="true" borders="rows" striped="false" style="font-size: 15pt; --table-cell-padding-block: 4pt; --table-cell-padding-inline: 8pt;"><tbody><tr><td><p>Input</p></td><td><p>Value and basis</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Machine</p></td><td><p>Rp 75,000,000</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Life and salvage</p></td><td><p>8 years; 10%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Depreciation</p></td><td><p>Rp 8,437,500/year</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Interest</p></td><td><p>8% × Rp 41,250,000 = Rp 3,300,000/year</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Housing and insurance</p></td><td><p>Rp 1,125,000/year</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Annual fixed cost</b></p></td><td><p><b>Rp 12,862,500/year</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Variable cost</p></td><td><p>Rp 380,000/ha</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p font-size="11pt">Depreciation method: <a href="https://files.ontario.ca/omafra-budgeting-farm-machinery-costs-20-007-en-2020-05-12.pdf">Ontario machinery-cost guide</a>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="9V_pOt_gAv" vertical-align="center" cell-style="subtle" colspan="24"><p role="eyebrow">Local custom rate</p><h3>Rp 700,000/ha</h3><p>12,862,500 ÷ (700,000 − 380,000) = <b>40.2 ha/year</b></p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="sm"><display size="md">20 ha</display><h4>served in year one</h4><p>Cost per hectare = <b>Rp 1,023,000/ha</b>, well above the rate charged.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="Eg3QGTklAJ" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="f_IghhF8Gr"><h2>The calendar, not the machine, was the binding constraint</h2><p>At 0.12 ha/hour, available days and daily working hours determine whether the machine can cross break-even.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="bvC9kWvE7j" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="outline">One village</label></labels><display size="md">28.8</display><h4>ha/year ceiling</h4><p>0.12 × 6 hours/day = 0.72 ha/day</p><p>0.72 × 20 days × 2 seasons = <b>28.8 ha/year</b></p><p>The ceiling is below the 40.2 ha/year break-even before any delay.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="s5aX67UmtN" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><labels><label variant="solid">Three-village schedule</label></labels><display size="md">48</display><h4>ha/year ceiling</h4><p>Staggered planting dates justify 8-hour days across a 25-day window.</p><p>0.12 × 8 × 25 × 2 = <b>48 ha/year</b></p><p>At 45 ha served, cost falls to <b>Rp 666,000/ha</b>, below the Rp 700,000/ha rate.</p></grid-item></grid><p><b>No new horsepower was purchased. Access to more working days created the gain.</b></p><p role="caption">Capacity basis: <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">Pinrang transplanter field test</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qibcIblE3G" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="PJg8Je84bn"><h2>Five strategies, in order of return per rupiah spent</h2><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="Wxv_eTzjI_" colspan="12"><h4>Raise utilization</h4><p>Share UPJA service across villages with staggered planting dates.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Gkdmffn4Ju" colspan="12"><h4>Train operators</h4><p>Improve turning discipline and clear blockages quickly.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BFJseDVdAE" colspan="12"><h4>Maintain preventively</h4><p>Protect the scheduled days that break-even depends on.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="o-ooIzJmx7" colspan="12"><h4>Right-size capacity</h4><p>Do not buy capacity the calendar cannot use.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="OYgUIZaaOm" colspan="12"><h4>Measure and record</h4><p>Use field logs rather than brochure capacity.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption"><span text-color="muted">Effective field capacity should come from actual area and field hours. Method: <a href="https://www.extension.iastate.edu/AgDM/crops/pdf/a3-24.pdf">Iowa State University Extension</a>.</span></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="hoqAyrKGJ7" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qBQLqZm3Y-"><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><h1>What to take back to the field</h1><p font-size="lg" style="padding-right: 22%;">Efficiency is a ratio you compute, not a quality the machine possesses.</p><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="9Omt6svP9X" colspan="20"><h3>Measure the field</h3><p>Field efficiency of 80–86% is realistic. Most of the missing share is geometry and logistics.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="tBOZw1CNWQ" colspan="20"><h3>Measure the denominator</h3><p>Annual use governs cost per hectare. Break-even area is the decisive figure before buying.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fLW_1UCb4H" colspan="20"><h3>Measure the outcome</h3><p>Mechanization pays through loss avoided and labor released, not speed alone.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="18pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Zmw_5u1KFq" background-color="accent" padding="16pt 20pt"><h3>First action</h3><p>Time one pass. Weigh one loss sample. Compare your cost per hectare with the local custom rate.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Evidence: <a href="https://jurnal.fp.unila.ac.id/index.php/JTP/article/download/4851/pdf">field efficiency</a> · <a href="https://eprints.unram.ac.id/31651/">harvest loss and production cost</a>.</p></grid-item></grid></section>